    45	We adopt a broad-spectrum approach to analyze such a large
    46	pool of mutated runs. For every mutated test run, we are able to
    47	determine: (a) if the mutation induced a state infection; (b) if the
    48	infection propagated through the end of the test run; and (c) if the
